    "body": "fix on issue/946-gouge-arcs-xz-yz · PR #971 · pinned by a_vertex_between_a_vertical_arcs_joints_past_the_floor_is_a_gouge, the_same_vertex_clear_of_the_floor_stays_clean, a_model_corner_between_a_vertical_arcs_joints_is_judged (crates/sim/tests/boundary_arc_planes.rs) + arc_wall_plane unit tests · merges when reviewed\n\nThe P1 argument does not hold, so per this issue's own rule the label is raised to P0. On an r 200 G18/G19 arc the joints (union of both chord sets) stand 1.92 mm apart along the projected line. A wall vertex 3.90 mm off the footprint (90 um past a 4 mm cutter's 3.99 mm floor) read >= 4.016 mm from every joint and passed without a warning. The pin fails without the fix (verdict `[]`) and convicts with it.",
